The internet is a long wire connecting computers together. Computers that stay online 24 hours to serve information are called servers, while user computers are called clients.
HTML - Defines content and structure of a website (images, textboxes, buttons, etc)
CSS - Styling a website
Javascript - Behavior of a website and allows it to do things
A website can exist solely with an HTML file but not a CSS or JS file on its own.

HTML stands for HyperText Markup Language

HyperText refers to links that connect web pages to others
Markup Language refers to HTML tags that are used to annotate content and define its structural role.

<h1></h1> - header tags
<p></p> - paragraph tags
<hr /> - horizontal line
<br /> - new line